{"case_id":"C018","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","input_semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["readHeaderMemTiff","pixCountArbInRect"],"reason":"H0 does not exercise the changed TIFF memory-header API at all, so it misses tag-dependent output-state behavior in readHeaderMemTiff. Its pixCountArbInRect call also fixes val to L_SET_WHITE and factor to 2, preventing systematic coverage of the new depth-dependent val validation boundaries.","evidence":["Both H0 targets accept only pixReadMemSpix(data, size); neither calls readHeaderMemTiff nor supplies in-memory TIFF data.","In S1, readHeaderMemTiff no longer initializes *pres to 300 or *pcmap to 0 before optional TIFF tag lookups, making caller-provided output state observable when resolution or TIFFTAG_COLORMAP is absent.","H0 calls pixCountArbInRect(pix_pointer_payload, box1, L_SET_WHITE, 2, &l_i) with fixed val and factor despite S1 adding val < 0 and val > (1 << d) - 1 checks based on pixGetDepth(pixs).","Although the SPIX payload can vary image depth, H0 cannot independently generate negative val, per-depth maximum values, or values just above those maxima."],"recommended_action":"Add a memory-TIFF target that calls readHeaderMemTiff with sentinel-initialized pres and pcmap outputs and varies missing/present resolution, colormap, compression, and directory tags. Also add or extend a pix3 target to vary val around -1, 0, (1 << d) - 1, and 1 << d for 1-, 2-, 4-, and 8-bpp PIX inputs, while varying factor across invalid and valid boundaries."}
